From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:41:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mt6771: drop vcodec_enc as well, it also points
 at &scp

The 7.3 SoC description gained a vcodec_enc node next to vcodec_dec, and
it carries the same mediatek,scp = <&scp> reference. The SCP node is
deleted for MT6771, so remove vcodec_enc too or dtc refuses to build
mt6771-fplus-t1100.dtb and mt6771-fplus-t800.dtb.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771.dtsi | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771.dtsi
index bd05fae03..417b480d0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771.dtsi
@@ -112,11 +112,13 @@ &pio {
 /delete-node/ &scp;
 
 /*
- * vcodec_dec points at &scp (mediatek,scp = <&scp>) and needs SCP firmware to
- * do anything useful; removing it keeps the tree consistent after the delete
- * above. There is no vcodec_enc node on MT8183 in 6.12.
+ * vcodec_dec/vcodec_enc point at &scp (mediatek,scp = <&scp>) and need SCP
+ * firmware to do anything useful; removing them keeps the tree consistent
+ * after the delete above. vcodec_enc appeared in the SoC description after
+ * 6.12 and has the same reference.
  */
 /delete-node/ &vcodec_dec;
+/delete-node/ &vcodec_enc;
 
 /*
  * Smart Voltage Scaling writes DVFS/thermal registers using efuse calibration
